<title>UK: Cypriot freighter still aground at Veracruz.</title>
<headline>Cypriot freighter still aground at Veracruz.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cyprus-flagged freighter Nika II which ran aground in gale force nine winds at Veracruz anchorage, Mexico, is still aground Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>An unsuccessful attempt was made to float the 15,251 dwt vessel and a second attempt will be made on February 24 or early 25 using a larger tug.</p>
<p>The Nika II sailed from Abidjan on January 23 and was inbound to Veracruz to load a cargo of bagged sugar for Algeria.</p>
</text>
